---
// Medical information (canvas: Medical.dc.html).
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/url';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Medical Screening for Ayahuasca and Psilocybin | MexiSol World"
  description="Who should not take ayahuasca, psilocybin or Satori, which medications interact, and how our health screening works before any retreat is confirmed."
  path="/medical"
  current="resources"
  ogImage="medical"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Medical information', path: '/medical' }]}
>
  <section class="section" style="padding-bottom:var(--space-8);border-bottom:1px solid var(--hairline)">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="label" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-5)">Resources</p>
      <h1 class="t-display" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-5)">Medical information</h1>
      <p class="t-lead" style="max-width:var(--measure)">These medicines are powerful and not right for every body. Read this before you book, and be honest with us on the call.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap grid">
      <div>
        <p class="label" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-5)">How screening works</p>
        <h2 class="t-heading" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-5)">Nothing is confirmed until we review your health</h2>
        <p class="muted" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-4)">When you register, we ask about your medical history, every medication, supplement and herb you take, and any recent use of other substances. We go over it with you on a call.</p>
        <p class="muted" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-4)">Some conditions mean the retreat is not safe for you. Others only need clearance from your own doctor, or a change in which medicines you take part in.</p>
        <p>Never stop a prescribed medication on your own. Any change should be planned with the doctor who prescribed it.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="label" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-5)">The ayahuasca retreat may not be safe if you have</h2>
        <ul class="rule-list">
          <li>Epilepsy or a seizure disorder</li>
          <li>Schizophrenia, psychosis, bipolar or a dissociative disorder</li>
          <li>Serious heart disease, a past heart attack, stents, arrhythmia or a pacemaker</li>
          <li>Severe liver disease</li>
          <li>A past stroke, brain bleed, aneurysm or blood clot</li>
          <li>Active dependence on alcohol, benzodiazepines or opioids</li>
          <li>An active eating disorder that involves purging, or a past tear in the esophagus</li>
          <li>An organ transplant or immune-suppressing medication</li>
          <li>Chemotherapy or radiation in the past four weeks</li>
          <li>Current or past use of growth hormone (HGH)</li>
          <li>A pregnancy, or you are breastfeeding</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--top-rule" id="psilocybin">
    <div class="wrap grid">
      <div>
        <p class="label" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-5)">Psilocybin</p>
        <h2 class="t-heading" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-5)">What we check before a psilocybin retreat</h2>
        <p class="muted" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-4)">Psilocybin is easier on the body than ayahuasca, but it is not right for everyone. Its main risk is psychological, so screening and preparation matter as much as the dose.</p>
        <p class="muted" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-4)">The psilocybin retreat also includes one Satori ceremony, which contains an MAO inhibitor. Everything on the ayahuasca list above applies to that night too.</p>
        <p class="t-caption muted">Based on MacCallum and colleagues, <a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9751063/">"Therapeutic use of psilocybin: practical considerations for dosing and administration"</a>, Frontiers in Psychiatry, 2022.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="label" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-5)">The psilocybin retreat may not be safe if you have</h3>
        <ul class="rule-list">
          <li>A personal history of schizophrenia, psychosis, bipolar disorder or borderline personality disorder</li>
          <li>A pregnancy, or you are breastfeeding</li>
          <li>Serious or uncontrolled heart disease or high blood pressure. Psilocybin raises heart rate and blood pressure for a few hours</li>
        </ul>
        <h3 class="label" style="margin:var(--space-7) 0 var(--space-5)">Tell us if you take</h3>
        <ul class="rule-list">
          <li>Antidepressants: SSRIs, SNRIs, tricyclics or MAOIs. Some can blunt or intensify the experience, and mixing serotonergic drugs carries a risk of serotonin syndrome</li>
          <li>Antipsychotics, lithium or stimulants</li>
          <li>Other drugs that act on serotonin or dopamine</li>
          <li>Diclofenac or probenecid, which may need to be paused before the ceremony</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section deep">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="label" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-5)">By medicine</p>
      <h2 class="t-heading" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-8)">What each one asks of you</h2>
      <div class="grid" style="--min:240px;--gap:var(--space-7)">
        <div class="rule-top"><h3 class="t-title" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-3)">Ayahuasca and Satori</h3><p>Ayahuasca contains MAOIs, which can react dangerously with many medicines and supplements. Satori is DMT from tepezcohuite bark with Syrian rue, also an MAO inhibitor, so the same review applies to both.</p></div>
        <div class="rule-top"><h3 class="t-title" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-3)">Psilocybin</h3><p>Gentler on the body, but serious liver disease is still a reason not to attend. Satori is part of this retreat too, so the medication review applies.</p></div>
        <div class="rule-top"><h3 class="t-title" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-3)">Kambo</h3><p>Not for anyone on medication for low blood pressure, with Addison's disease, or who has taken Bufo in the past eight weeks.</p></div>
        <div class="rule-top"><h3 class="t-title" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-3)">Bufo</h3><p>An optional add-on at extra cost, and always your choice. Everything on the list above applies.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap grid">
      <div>
        <p class="label" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-5)">Medications</p>
        <h2 class="t-heading" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-5)">Tell us about everything you take</h2>
        <p class="muted" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-4)">Some medicines are fine to keep taking. Many are not. The groups below are the most common problems. The list is not complete, which is why we ask for everything.</p>
        <p class="muted">Cannabis can blunt the experience, so we ask you to stop it before you come.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="rule-list">
        <li>Antidepressants, including all SSRIs, SNRIs, tricyclics and MAOIs</li>
        <li>Benzodiazepines, sleeping pills and many antipsychotics</li>
        <li>ADHD stimulants and weight-loss drugs</li>
        <li>Opioid painkillers and tramadol</li>
        <li>Migraine triptans, some antihistamines and decongestants, cough syrup with dextromethorphan</li>
        <li>Herbs and supplements: St. John's Wort, 5-HTP, kava, kratom, ginseng, rhodiola, ephedra, yohimbe</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="gutter center" style="padding-bottom:var(--space-9)">
    <div class="measure rule-top rule-top--soft" style="padding-top:var(--space-8)">
      <h2 class="t-heading" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-5)">Not sure about something?</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-7)">Ask us before you book. We would rather talk it through than have you arrive unsure.</p>
      <div class="cluster">
        <Button href={href('/book-a-call')} data-track="book_call">Book a call</Button>
        <Button href={href('/prepare')}>Prepare and travel</Button>
      </div>
      <p class="t-caption muted" style="margin-top:var(--space-6)">This page is general information, not medical advice.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
